Package: emlR
Title: All Elementary Functions From a Single Binary Operator
Version: 0.1.0.9000
Authors@R:
    person("Philipp", "Thoss", , "ph.thoss@gmx.de", role = c("aut", "cre"),
           comment = c(ORCID = "0000-0002-4672-2792"))
Description: An R implementation of the EML (Exp-Minus-Log) Sheffer
    operator from Odrzywolek (2026, arXiv:2603.21852), which proves that
    a single binary operator eml(x, y) = exp(x) - log(y), together with
    the constant 1, generates all elementary functions. The package
    provides the operator, native R-AST identity catalog, peephole
    simplifier with two modes (stays-in-EML and collapses-to-base-R),
    a stack-machine bytecode compiler for vectorised evaluation, and
    a depth-n master formula with L-BFGS-B fitter for symbolic regression.
